  "intro_html": "<p>The Churfirsten range of seven mountains between Walensee and Toggenburg, is unique. On the north side they form a precisely arranged row of monopitch slopes and on the south they are sheer cliffs offering a splendid view down to Walensee almost 2000 metres down. Hiking to one of them is a must for every alpine hiker. The question is: which one? We have chosen Zuestoll for its elegant form. The ascent is short and multifaceted. It offers a number of exposed, but well-equipped passages and the aforementioned view.</p>\n<p>The summit ascent is now marked white-blue; it had been white-red until recently.</p>",
